.TH FANI 1 "August 2026" "fani 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fani \- continuous Markdown translation for Git and GitHub
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fani
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
fani reads Markdown from an immutable Git revision, reuses trusted translation memory from SQLite, delegates unresolved units to a built-in model provider or isolated custom Agent command, verifies assembled output, and can publish stable language branches and GitHub pull requests.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create a safe starter configuration for a built-in provider.
.TP
.B sync
Translate, verify, recover, materialize, and optionally publish pending work.
.TP
.B status
Plan from an immutable Git revision without calling an Agent.
.TP
.B check
Run the CI-friendly read-only planning and check path.
.TP
.B doctor
Validate configuration and runtime prerequisites.
.TP
.B adopt
Validate and adopt divergent human target files.
.TP
.B discard
Restore canonical verified target files over divergent human edits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Use PATH as the configuration file. The default is fani.toml.
.TP
.BI --repo " NAME_OR_PATH"
Select one configured repository.
.TP
.BI --lang " LANGUAGE"
Select one configured language, or set the initial target language for init.
.TP
.BI --provider " PROVIDER"
Select the built-in provider for init: anthropic, openai, xai, or deepseek.
.TP
.BI --model " MODEL"
Set the provider model for init.
.TP
.B --force
Allow init to replace an existing configuration.
.TP
.BI --report-dir " PATH"
Write sync reports under PATH.
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress sync progress and report-location output.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print help.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means up to date or successfully completed; 1 means human action is required; 2 means an infrastructure or configuration error; 3 means a bounded batch completed with deferred work remaining.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I fani.toml
Configuration file.
.TP
.I <repo>/<data_dir>/fani.db
Authoritative SQLite state for a configured repository.
.SH SEE ALSO
The annotated configuration example and systemd user units are included in the release archive.
